==================================================
19. TESTING REQUIREMENTS
==================================================

Test the complete application.

At minimum, test these scenarios:

TEST 1:
A customer registers, signs out, signs in again, and retrieves
their existing account information.

TEST 2:
A seller creates a store and publishes a real product.

TEST 3:
Another customer sees the published product.

TEST 4:
A customer follows a store.

TEST 5:
The customer closes the application, signs in on another
device or browser, and still sees that store as followed.

TEST 6:
The customer unfollows the store and the relationship is
correctly updated.

TEST 7:
A customer adds a product to the cart and retrieves the cart
after signing in again.

TEST 8:
A customer submits an eligible review and the review is
stored and displayed correctly.

TEST 9:
A buyer sends a message to a seller and both authorized
participants can retrieve the conversation.

TEST 10:
A new message creates a persistent notification.

TEST 11:
A real test payment is verified by the backend before the
order is marked as paid.

TEST 12:
A failed payment does not produce a false successful order.

TEST 13:
A seller cannot access another seller's private orders.

TEST 14:
A customer cannot access another customer's private account
data or conversations.

TEST 15:
Two customers attempting to purchase the last unit do not
cause unintended overselling.

TEST 16:
A seller updates a product price and checkout correctly
revalidates the amount.

TEST 17:
The administrator can moderate listings and manage users
only through authorized operations.

TEST 18:
The application builds successfully and critical user flows
work without console or server errors.

Use automated tests where practical.

Do not claim that cross-device synchronization, payments,
messaging, or notifications have been tested unless the
corresponding tests were actually performed.

